All check logic, warning codes (SCxxxx), warning and fix messages, optional
check descriptions, directive and configuration semantics, and output formats
derive from ShellCheck. The wiki URLs that the tool prints
(https://www.shellcheck.net/wiki/) point to the upstream ShellCheck wiki.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived files
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Each derived Rust source file names its upstream source in its header, for
example:

    // Port of ShellCheck src/ShellCheck/Analytics.hs `checkEchoWc`, lines 483-494 (e11f964)

To list the derived files and their upstream sources:

    grep -rn -m1 'Port of' crates/

Some files do not have such a header, such as crate roots and the test
files. These can still contain material from ShellCheck, for example tests
ported from its prop_ tests. Treat everything under crates/ as derived from
ShellCheck unless its header says otherwise.

The correspondence by crate:

    crates/core/        AST.hs, ASTLib.hs, Interface.hs, Data.hs, Prelude.hs,
                        Regex.hs
    crates/parser/      Parser.hs
    crates/analyzer/    Analyzer.hs, AnalyzerLib.hs, CFG.hs, CFGAnalysis.hs
    crates/checks/      Analytics.hs, Checks/Commands.hs, Checks/ShellSupport.hs
                        (one file per check)
    crates/checker/     Checker.hs, EditorConfig.hs, and the EditorConfig
                        lookup from shellcheck.hs
    crates/formatter/   Formatter/*.hs, Fixer.hs
    crates/cli/         shellcheck.hs

Files whose header says "no Haskell counterpart" (for example the
conformance harness in crates/conformance/) are original to this project.
They are part of the same GPL-licensed work.

corpus/tests.jsonl and corpus/checks.json contain test scripts and test
sources extracted verbatim from ShellCheck's prop_ unit tests, together with
the output of the real ShellCheck binary on those scripts (oracle_codes).
corpus/tasks.json is derived from ShellCheck's check registration lists.

